1
00:00:00,533 --> 00:00:02,000
You open your bills at the end of the month

2
00:00:02,333 --> 00:00:04,400
The sharpest thing is not the smaller balance

3
00:00:04,466 --> 00:00:05,833
It is the sudden realization

4
00:00:05,966 --> 00:00:07,633
It is not that you do not understand finance

5
00:00:07,666 --> 00:00:08,933
It is that you never noticed

6
00:00:08,933 --> 00:00:10,733
Life has been doing the math for you

7
00:00:10,733 --> 00:00:11,866
Your salary just arrives

8
00:00:11,933 --> 00:00:13,300
Rent takes one piece first

9
00:00:13,300 --> 00:00:14,666
The credit card takes another

10
00:00:14,666 --> 00:00:16,166
A few memberships quietly renew

11
00:00:16,166 --> 00:00:18,100
Your balance feels gently pressed down

12
00:00:18,100 --> 00:00:20,133
Many people think finance is hard because of math

13
00:00:20,133 --> 00:00:22,133
But where ordinary people really lose out

14
00:00:22,133 --> 00:00:23,733
Is never in failing to calculate formulas

15
00:00:23,733 --> 00:00:24,566
It is not seeing

16
00:00:24,566 --> 00:00:25,733
When money comes in

17
00:00:25,733 --> 00:00:26,533
When money goes out

18
00:00:26,533 --> 00:00:28,800
And when it claims your future self in advance

19
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:30,800
You think interest rates live at the bank counter

20
00:00:30,800 --> 00:00:32,166
Inflation lives in the news

21
00:00:32,166 --> 00:00:33,900
Cash flow lives in company reports

22
00:00:33,900 --> 00:00:36,133
But they are all inside your daily choices

23
00:00:36,133 --> 00:00:37,200
Whether to order takeout

24
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:38,266
Whether to renew a membership

25
00:00:38,266 --> 00:00:39,766
Whether to buy a phone in installments

26
00:00:39,766 --> 00:00:41,766
Whether a salary delayed three days would scare you

27
00:00:41,800 --> 00:00:43,866
These are the real finance scenes for ordinary people

28
00:00:43,866 --> 00:00:45,333
Ordinary people do not understand finance

29
00:00:45,333 --> 00:00:46,400
Not because they cannot calculate

30
00:00:46,400 --> 00:00:47,533
But because they have not seen

31
00:00:47,533 --> 00:00:50,166
Life has quietly changed the way it prices things

32
00:00:50,200 --> 00:00:51,633
Have you ever felt this

33
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:53,333
Before you left home with 100 yuan

34
00:00:53,333 --> 00:00:54,400
You could still have a meal

35
00:00:54,533 --> 00:00:55,466
Buy a milk tea

36
00:00:55,700 --> 00:00:57,333
And bring some fruit home

37
00:00:57,566 --> 00:00:59,433
Now 100 yuan just enters your phone

38
00:00:59,500 --> 00:01:00,633
A taxi costs over ten

39
00:01:00,666 --> 00:01:01,766
Lunch costs over thirty

40
00:01:01,766 --> 00:01:02,833
Coffee costs over twenty

41
00:01:02,900 --> 00:01:04,233
Order takeout at night

42
00:01:04,333 --> 00:01:06,200
And it disappears like tissues pulled from a box

43
00:01:06,300 --> 00:01:07,466
It is not that you never keep accounts

44
00:01:07,566 --> 00:01:08,800
It is not that you spend wildly

45
00:01:08,966 --> 00:01:11,033
You just notice something awkward

46
00:01:11,266 --> 00:01:12,600
Your income seems to still be there

47
00:01:12,700 --> 00:01:14,566
But life has more resistance

48
00:01:14,600 --> 00:01:15,800
When many people meet this

49
00:01:15,800 --> 00:01:17,166
Their first reaction is to blame themselves

50
00:01:17,366 --> 00:01:18,533
Am I too lazy

51
00:01:18,533 --> 00:01:19,633
Am I too greedy

52
00:01:19,766 --> 00:01:21,433
Am I just bad at living carefully

53
00:01:21,566 --> 00:01:22,966
But think about it carefully

54
00:01:23,100 --> 00:01:24,600
The places you spend money every day

55
00:01:24,600 --> 00:01:26,366
Many are not happy consumption

56
00:01:26,500 --> 00:01:28,533
They are to keep life running

57
00:01:28,700 --> 00:01:30,033
Rent is not a reward

58
00:01:30,066 --> 00:01:31,400
Commuting is not enjoyment

59
00:01:31,500 --> 00:01:32,800
Lunch is not luxury

60
00:01:32,900 --> 00:01:34,600
A phone plan is not showing off

61
00:01:34,700 --> 00:01:36,366
They are more like a row of small gates

62
00:01:36,500 --> 00:01:37,833
Opening at fixed times every day

63
00:01:37,933 --> 00:01:39,666
Letting your money out bit by bit

64
00:01:39,700 --> 00:01:42,400
This is where finance most easily misleads people

65
00:01:42,533 --> 00:01:43,966
It sounds like stocks

66
00:01:43,966 --> 00:01:44,800
Like funds

67
00:01:44,966 --> 00:01:46,666
Like piles of curves and numbers

68
00:01:46,766 --> 00:01:48,200
But for ordinary people

69
00:01:48,300 --> 00:01:50,066
The first place finance touches you

70
00:01:50,066 --> 00:01:51,333
Is not an investment account

71
00:01:51,366 --> 00:01:52,866
It is that balance at the end of the month

72
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:54,433
You watch the balance shrink

73
00:01:54,533 --> 00:01:55,866
And your chest tightens for a second

74
00:01:55,900 --> 00:01:57,933
That is the sound of finance inside life

75
00:01:58,100 --> 00:02:00,333
It is not testing your math at a blackboard

76
00:02:00,566 --> 00:02:01,600
It is asking you

77
00:02:01,600 --> 00:02:03,000
When does your money come in

78
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:03,933
When does it go out

79
00:02:03,966 --> 00:02:06,333
And whether there is room to breathe in between

80
00:02:06,466 --> 00:02:07,733
You may not understand finance

81
00:02:07,800 --> 00:02:09,633
Not because you cannot understand numbers

82
00:02:09,733 --> 00:02:11,400
But because nobody ever told you

83
00:02:11,500 --> 00:02:12,666
Money is not a number

84
00:02:12,800 --> 00:02:14,333
Money is a moving river

85
00:02:14,533 --> 00:02:15,800
The water may look plentiful

86
00:02:15,866 --> 00:02:17,633
But if every outlet is leaking

87
00:02:17,733 --> 00:02:18,833
Standing by the river

88
00:02:18,900 --> 00:02:20,266
You will still feel thirsty

89
00:02:20,600 --> 00:02:21,600
On a Friday night

90
00:02:21,600 --> 00:02:22,833
You have dinner with friends

91
00:02:22,966 --> 00:02:23,800
Someone says

92
00:02:23,933 --> 00:02:25,866
My salary this month is actually fine

93
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:27,766
I just do not know where the money went

94
00:02:27,866 --> 00:02:29,066
That sentence is very ordinary

95
00:02:29,166 --> 00:02:31,133
But behind it is cash flow

96
00:02:31,400 --> 00:02:34,233
Cash flow sounds like something only bosses care about

97
00:02:34,400 --> 00:02:35,566
In plain words

98
00:02:35,600 --> 00:02:38,033
It is the rhythm of money coming in and going out

99
00:02:38,266 --> 00:02:39,566
When money comes in a little earlier

100
00:02:39,566 --> 00:02:40,666
And goes out a little slower

101
00:02:40,666 --> 00:02:41,766
You have room

102
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:43,300
When money comes in a little later

103
00:02:43,300 --> 00:02:44,466
And goes out a little faster

104
00:02:44,466 --> 00:02:45,533
You begin to panic

105
00:02:45,666 --> 00:02:47,000
With the same monthly salary of 8000

106
00:02:47,166 --> 00:02:49,366
Two people may feel completely different

107
00:02:49,533 --> 00:02:50,766
One person lives with family

108
00:02:50,800 --> 00:02:52,466
Fixed monthly expenses are 2000

109
00:02:52,666 --> 00:02:53,766
After the salary arrives

110
00:02:53,766 --> 00:02:55,366
There is still 6000 to arrange

111
00:02:55,533 --> 00:02:56,733
Another person rents

112
00:02:56,800 --> 00:02:57,833
Rent is 3000

113
00:02:57,866 --> 00:02:58,866
Commuting is 500

114
00:02:58,866 --> 00:02:59,933
Food is 2000

115
00:03:00,100 --> 00:03:02,233
Plus the phone bought in installments before

116
00:03:02,400 --> 00:03:03,466
The salary just arrives

117
00:03:03,466 --> 00:03:05,333
And half of it already does not belong to them

118
00:03:05,600 --> 00:03:07,100
These two people have the same income

119
00:03:07,100 --> 00:03:08,733
But their days are completely different

120
00:03:08,800 --> 00:03:10,433
The difference is not who works harder

121
00:03:10,466 --> 00:03:12,266
It is that the cash flow pressure is different

122
00:03:12,266 --> 00:03:13,233
You will notice

123
00:03:13,300 --> 00:03:14,333
Many peoples anxiety

124
00:03:14,333 --> 00:03:16,333
Is not because they are so poor they have nothing

125
00:03:16,333 --> 00:03:18,066
It is because their money has no buffer

126
00:03:18,200 --> 00:03:20,533
Like a phone with only 5 percent battery left

127
00:03:20,666 --> 00:03:21,566
It can still light up

128
00:03:21,566 --> 00:03:23,000
It can still open apps

129
00:03:23,100 --> 00:03:25,066
But you no longer dare to tap freely

130
00:03:25,166 --> 00:03:26,900
You stare at the battery without noticing

131
00:03:26,900 --> 00:03:27,800
You stare at outlets

132
00:03:27,800 --> 00:03:29,200
You stare at every bit of power used

133
00:03:29,400 --> 00:03:30,533
Money is the same

134
00:03:30,566 --> 00:03:32,133
When your cash flow is too tight

135
00:03:32,166 --> 00:03:33,600
It is not that you do not want to choose

136
00:03:33,600 --> 00:03:34,866
It is that you do not dare to choose

137
00:03:35,066 --> 00:03:36,600
A friend asks you out on the weekend

138
00:03:36,600 --> 00:03:38,266
You first think of transport and meal costs

139
00:03:38,366 --> 00:03:39,666
An appliance at home breaks

140
00:03:39,666 --> 00:03:41,600
You first wonder if it can wait until next month

141
00:03:41,733 --> 00:03:43,133
Someone recommends a course

142
00:03:43,266 --> 00:03:44,833
You know it may be useful

143
00:03:44,900 --> 00:03:46,766
But you stop on the payment page for a long time

144
00:03:46,966 --> 00:03:48,066
This is not being stingy

145
00:03:48,200 --> 00:03:49,766
This is the system reminding you

146
00:03:49,766 --> 00:03:51,066
Your water level is too low

147
00:03:51,300 --> 00:03:53,033
So for ordinary people to understand finance

148
00:03:53,133 --> 00:03:55,066
The first step is not studying how to get rich

149
00:03:55,266 --> 00:03:57,966
It is seeing whether you have room to breathe

150
00:03:58,166 --> 00:03:59,866
Does a payment make you lighter

151
00:03:59,966 --> 00:04:01,766
Or make next month you tighter

152
00:04:01,866 --> 00:04:03,866
This reaches you earlier than yield rates

153
00:04:03,900 --> 00:04:06,233
And it is more honest than any complex formula

154
00:04:06,400 --> 00:04:08,800
Many elders ask whether you have savings

155
00:04:08,900 --> 00:04:10,566
As a kid you may have found it annoying

156
00:04:10,733 --> 00:04:12,166
As if they only cared about money

157
00:04:12,333 --> 00:04:13,600
But from another angle

158
00:04:13,700 --> 00:04:15,466
They are not asking about a number

159
00:04:15,566 --> 00:04:18,066
They are asking whether your life has a buffer

160
00:04:18,300 --> 00:04:19,566
If your tooth suddenly hurts

161
00:04:19,700 --> 00:04:21,133
And a hospital visit costs 1000

162
00:04:21,266 --> 00:04:23,200
Will it immediately affect your rent

163
00:04:23,333 --> 00:04:25,366
If your company pays salary a few days late

164
00:04:25,466 --> 00:04:27,333
Will you immediately start borrowing money

165
00:04:27,533 --> 00:04:28,833
If your phone breaks

166
00:04:28,933 --> 00:04:30,533
Can you fix it and move on

167
00:04:30,533 --> 00:04:33,000
Or will this small thing trap your whole month

168
00:04:33,133 --> 00:04:34,233
A buffer is something

169
00:04:34,400 --> 00:04:35,566
You usually cannot see

170
00:04:35,700 --> 00:04:37,833
Only when trouble comes do you know if it is there

171
00:04:37,966 --> 00:04:39,133
When you have a buffer

172
00:04:39,300 --> 00:04:40,600
Trouble is just trouble

173
00:04:40,733 --> 00:04:41,966
When you have no buffer

174
00:04:42,133 --> 00:04:43,666
Trouble turns into a crisis

175
00:04:43,800 --> 00:04:46,400
That is why many people with decent income

176
00:04:46,466 --> 00:04:48,566
Cannot handle even a small disturbance

177
00:04:48,666 --> 00:04:49,766
It is not that they are fragile

178
00:04:49,866 --> 00:04:51,433
It is that their cash flow is too thin

179
00:04:51,966 --> 00:04:53,433
You stand in a mall

180
00:04:53,800 --> 00:04:55,166
You see a phone you like

181
00:04:55,500 --> 00:04:56,566
The original price is 6000

182
00:04:56,733 --> 00:04:58,833
The page says 12 interest free installments

183
00:04:59,133 --> 00:05:00,200
500 each month

184
00:05:00,500 --> 00:05:03,066
At that moment the price suddenly becomes smaller

185
00:05:03,300 --> 00:05:04,766
6000 yuan feels scary

186
00:05:04,933 --> 00:05:06,600
500 yuan feels like you can grit your teeth

187
00:05:06,933 --> 00:05:09,400
This is where finance is best at magic

188
00:05:09,600 --> 00:05:11,333
It may not change the total price

189
00:05:11,466 --> 00:05:12,466
What it changes

190
00:05:12,500 --> 00:05:14,366
Is when you feel the price

191
00:05:14,700 --> 00:05:16,133
Interest rates in plain words

192
00:05:16,166 --> 00:05:17,633
Are the price of time

193
00:05:17,933 --> 00:05:19,366
You do not have 6000 today

194
00:05:19,466 --> 00:05:21,266
But you want to use the phone today

195
00:05:21,500 --> 00:05:24,233
So you move part of your next 12 months salary

196
00:05:24,333 --> 00:05:25,866
Forward into today

197
00:05:26,133 --> 00:05:28,033
That sounds like a finance class

198
00:05:28,166 --> 00:05:29,500
But back in daily life

199
00:05:29,500 --> 00:05:31,400
It is a very ordinary action

200
00:05:31,566 --> 00:05:33,533
Today you take the thing first

201
00:05:33,600 --> 00:05:35,533
Future you pays it back month by month

202
00:05:35,800 --> 00:05:38,133
If this thing truly helps you work

203
00:05:38,166 --> 00:05:39,333
Helps you save time

204
00:05:39,400 --> 00:05:40,933
Helps you earn more money back

205
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:42,633
Then it may be worth it

206
00:05:42,800 --> 00:05:45,166
But if it only makes today feel good

207
00:05:45,300 --> 00:05:46,733
And tomorrow it already feels old

208
00:05:46,766 --> 00:05:47,800
Then 500 a month

209
00:05:47,800 --> 00:05:48,966
Is not small money

210
00:05:49,133 --> 00:05:50,400
It is a thin string

211
00:05:50,600 --> 00:05:52,566
Tied lightly to your future salary

212
00:05:52,700 --> 00:05:53,933
Inflation is the same

213
00:05:54,066 --> 00:05:55,800
It is not just a word in the news

214
00:05:56,066 --> 00:05:56,866
In plain words

215
00:05:56,966 --> 00:05:58,000
The same money

216
00:05:58,000 --> 00:05:59,966
Buys back fewer things

217
00:06:00,100 --> 00:06:01,333
You did not work less hard

218
00:06:01,366 --> 00:06:03,466
Your salary number may still be the same

219
00:06:03,566 --> 00:06:05,800
But breakfast goes from 6 to 8

220
00:06:05,933 --> 00:06:08,233
Rent goes from 2800 to 3200

221
00:06:08,333 --> 00:06:10,433
A haircut goes from 35 to 50

222
00:06:10,600 --> 00:06:12,933
Every month feels like standing on an escalator

223
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:14,466
The escalator keeps moving down

224
00:06:14,533 --> 00:06:15,566
Even if you stand still

225
00:06:15,566 --> 00:06:16,933
You slowly move backward

226
00:06:17,066 --> 00:06:18,466
This sounds a bit annoying

227
00:06:18,600 --> 00:06:20,966
But it explains a very common grievance

228
00:06:21,100 --> 00:06:22,966
Why am I clearly not spending wildly

229
00:06:23,066 --> 00:06:24,733
Yet money feels tighter and tighter

230
00:06:24,933 --> 00:06:26,600
It is not that you suddenly got worse

231
00:06:26,600 --> 00:06:29,033
It is time repricing your money

232
00:06:29,266 --> 00:06:30,933
Your salary stands still

233
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:33,000
Other things move one step forward

234
00:06:33,100 --> 00:06:34,433
Risk works the same way

235
00:06:34,500 --> 00:06:36,966
It is not the red curve in an investing app

236
00:06:37,133 --> 00:06:38,800
It is the future suddenly reaching out

237
00:06:38,800 --> 00:06:40,600
And disrupting your plans today

238
00:06:40,766 --> 00:06:43,066
You think you only rented a place

239
00:06:43,266 --> 00:06:45,633
But you also bought commuting time

240
00:06:45,700 --> 00:06:46,733
Nearby prices

241
00:06:46,733 --> 00:06:47,933
The trouble of moving

242
00:06:47,966 --> 00:06:49,533
And the chance of a rent increase

243
00:06:49,800 --> 00:06:52,066
You think you only accepted a job

244
00:06:52,266 --> 00:06:54,833
But you also accepted the salary payment rhythm

245
00:06:54,933 --> 00:06:56,000
Industry changes

246
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:57,133
Overtime intensity

247
00:06:57,166 --> 00:06:58,933
And if income suddenly stops

248
00:06:58,933 --> 00:07:00,233
How long you can hold on

249
00:07:00,366 --> 00:07:02,533
These things do not look like finance

250
00:07:02,666 --> 00:07:04,433
But they all ask the same question

251
00:07:04,800 --> 00:07:06,133
Will this choice today

252
00:07:06,200 --> 00:07:08,400
Leave future you with fewer choices

253
00:07:08,500 --> 00:07:10,533
Finance does not make life complicated

254
00:07:10,700 --> 00:07:13,400
Finance shines a light on the hidden prices

255
00:07:13,400 --> 00:07:14,766
That were already inside life

256
00:07:14,766 --> 00:07:16,066
When you hear interest rates

257
00:07:16,133 --> 00:07:17,433
Do not only think of banks

258
00:07:17,600 --> 00:07:19,600
Think of that phone bought in installments

259
00:07:19,733 --> 00:07:21,033
When you hear inflation

260
00:07:21,133 --> 00:07:22,400
Do not only think of news

261
00:07:22,533 --> 00:07:25,433
Think of that small price raise sign at the breakfast stall

262
00:07:25,566 --> 00:07:26,866
When you hear risk

263
00:07:26,966 --> 00:07:28,666
Do not only think of investment losses

264
00:07:28,766 --> 00:07:30,833
Think of salary being three days late

265
00:07:30,900 --> 00:07:32,800
And whether your heart would suddenly feel hollow

266
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:34,633
When these images come together

267
00:07:34,666 --> 00:07:37,333
They are the finance ordinary people truly need to understand

268
00:07:37,766 --> 00:07:39,566
Next time before you pay

269
00:07:39,933 --> 00:07:41,233
Do not rush to scold yourself

270
00:07:41,400 --> 00:07:42,800
And do not rush to comfort yourself

271
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:45,333
You can ask three small questions in your mind

272
00:07:45,700 --> 00:07:47,400
When will this money go out

273
00:07:47,566 --> 00:07:48,800
Will it come back

274
00:07:48,966 --> 00:07:50,800
Will it press down next month me

275
00:07:51,133 --> 00:07:52,766
These three questions are not fancy

276
00:07:52,866 --> 00:07:53,833
But they work

277
00:07:54,133 --> 00:07:55,400
You buy a cup of coffee

278
00:07:55,500 --> 00:07:56,366
The money goes out

279
00:07:56,400 --> 00:07:57,533
It will not come back

280
00:07:57,700 --> 00:07:59,766
But it may buy half an hour of clarity

281
00:08:00,066 --> 00:08:02,233
If you truly need that half hour that day

282
00:08:02,333 --> 00:08:03,533
Then it is not waste

283
00:08:03,600 --> 00:08:04,733
You buy a course

284
00:08:04,800 --> 00:08:05,733
The money goes out

285
00:08:05,766 --> 00:08:07,266
It will not automatically come back

286
00:08:07,466 --> 00:08:09,366
Only when you truly use it to make something

287
00:08:09,500 --> 00:08:10,400
Write an article

288
00:08:10,400 --> 00:08:11,333
Build a plan

289
00:08:11,333 --> 00:08:12,633
Solve a work problem

290
00:08:12,866 --> 00:08:14,200
Does it have a chance to return

291
00:08:14,333 --> 00:08:15,933
You buy a phone in installments

292
00:08:16,100 --> 00:08:18,266
The money seems to go out only a little each month

293
00:08:18,333 --> 00:08:20,433
But it will press on you for 12 months straight

294
00:08:20,600 --> 00:08:22,400
The question is not whether you can buy it

295
00:08:22,500 --> 00:08:23,966
It is whether for the next 12 months

296
00:08:23,966 --> 00:08:27,000
I am willing to make room every month for todays decision

297
00:08:27,166 --> 00:08:28,133
You will notice

298
00:08:28,200 --> 00:08:29,833
What really makes people passive

299
00:08:29,966 --> 00:08:31,400
Is often not one big payment

300
00:08:31,500 --> 00:08:33,800
But a pile of small promises that do not hurt at first

301
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:35,366
A 19 point 9 membership

302
00:08:35,400 --> 00:08:37,033
A 39 point 9 speed up pack

303
00:08:37,133 --> 00:08:38,566
A few hundred each month in installments

304
00:08:38,733 --> 00:08:41,366
A dinner you felt too embarrassed to refuse

305
00:08:41,533 --> 00:08:43,366
On their own they are not scary

306
00:08:43,466 --> 00:08:44,800
But when they line up together

307
00:08:44,800 --> 00:08:46,966
They fill up your next month in advance

308
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:48,566
At that moment what you should look at

309
00:08:48,566 --> 00:08:50,366
Is not whether each payment is expensive

310
00:08:50,466 --> 00:08:51,933
But whether together

311
00:08:51,966 --> 00:08:54,333
They take away your choices next month

312
00:08:54,366 --> 00:08:55,733
The most tiring moment for a person

313
00:08:55,900 --> 00:08:57,333
Is often not having no money to spend

314
00:08:57,466 --> 00:08:58,733
It is that before the money arrives

315
00:08:58,800 --> 00:09:00,633
Its destination has already been arranged

316
00:09:00,966 --> 00:09:02,266
Ordinary people study finance

317
00:09:02,366 --> 00:09:04,366
Not to turn life into a spreadsheet

318
00:09:04,500 --> 00:09:06,866
And not to haggle over every yuan

319
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:08,733
But to see one more layer

320
00:09:08,766 --> 00:09:10,066
In the second before paying

321
00:09:10,400 --> 00:09:11,733
What this money buys

322
00:09:11,733 --> 00:09:12,933
Is it really an object

323
00:09:13,100 --> 00:09:14,666
Or is it a trouble being moved elsewhere

324
00:09:14,933 --> 00:09:16,600
Does it make future me freer

325
00:09:16,600 --> 00:09:18,466
Or leave future me with fewer choices

326
00:09:18,533 --> 00:09:20,200
If finance is spoken in human language

327
00:09:20,333 --> 00:09:21,833
It is actually this kind of judgment

328
00:09:21,966 --> 00:09:23,933
It may not make you rich right away

329
00:09:24,066 --> 00:09:26,433
But it will make you feel less inexplicably tight

330
00:09:26,533 --> 00:09:28,600
Less regret that only appears at month end

331
00:09:28,700 --> 00:09:30,200
Less of that grievance of working hard

332
00:09:30,200 --> 00:09:32,466
Yet not knowing where the money leaked away

333
00:09:32,700 --> 00:09:34,933
So ordinary people do not understand finance

334
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:36,633
Really not because they are bad at math

335
00:09:36,733 --> 00:09:38,466
But because from childhood to adulthood

336
00:09:38,533 --> 00:09:40,333
Many people were only taught how to calculate prices

337
00:09:40,366 --> 00:09:42,033
Not how to look at time

338
00:09:42,100 --> 00:09:43,200
How to look at risk

339
00:09:43,200 --> 00:09:44,566
How to look at their future self

340
00:09:44,733 --> 00:09:46,333
Next time you open your bills again

341
00:09:46,400 --> 00:09:48,400
And see your balance deducted bit by bit

342
00:09:48,533 --> 00:09:50,333
Do not rush to blame yourself

343
00:09:50,500 --> 00:09:51,466
Just pause for a few seconds

344
00:09:51,666 --> 00:09:53,233
Look behind those deductions

345
00:09:53,266 --> 00:09:55,266
Which one is taking care of today you

346
00:09:55,333 --> 00:09:57,433
Which one is squeezing next month you

347
00:09:57,466 --> 00:09:58,666
Once you can see this

348
00:09:58,733 --> 00:10:00,833
Finance is no longer a distant class

349
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:03,200
It becomes a small lamp beside your hand

350
00:10:03,366 --> 00:10:04,166
Not dazzling

351
00:10:04,266 --> 00:10:05,666
But enough before you pay

352
00:10:05,766 --> 00:10:07,166
To see the next step under your feet
